2.18 Debugging: Read the Evidence
A disciplined process is:

read the final error message;
identify the line that failed;
inspect the relevant object;
form a hypothesis;
test the smallest correction;
verify that the correction solves the analytical problem, not merely the syntax.







TipA Traceback Is Evidence



Do not treat an error message as noise to paste immediately into an AI assistant. Read it first.

